@startuml
title Availability emulation -- components (design 040)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "sdmx-proxy-config" {
  [AvailabilityEndpointConfiguration] as AEC
  [AvailabilityEmulationConfiguration] as AEMC
  [AvailabilityEmulationType\nNONE | DATA_QUERY] as TYPE
  [UnfilteredAvailabilitySource\nCONTENT_CONSTRAINT | PROBE] as UNFSRC
  [AvailabilityFixtureType\n+ DROP_TIME_PERIOD_KEY_VALUE\n+ KEEP_FIRST_CUBE_REGION] as FIX
  [ConfigValidator] as CV
}

AEC --> AEMC : emulation
AEMC --> TYPE
AEMC --> UNFSRC
AEC --> FIX : fixtures
CV ..> AEMC : rejects\n- type != NONE && availabilityEnabled\n- CONTENT_CONSTRAINT && constraint type\n  not in supportedStructures\n- probeFormat not in supportedFormats\n- probeDetail set on SDMX_3_0\n- supportsLimit=false && availabilityEnabled=false

package "sdmx-proxy :: controller" {
  [AvailabilityQuery30Controller] as CTL
}

package "sdmx-proxy :: services.adapter" {
  [AdapterRouterImpl] as ROUTER
  [GenericRegistryAdapter] as ADAPTER
  [StreamingAvailabilityConversionService\n+ write(Artefacts, OutputStream, MediaType)] as CONV
  [AvailabilityFixtureService] as FIXSVC
  [ContentConstraintMapper] as CCM
}

package "sdmx-proxy :: services.availability  (new)" {
  interface AvailabilityEmulator
  [AvailabilityEmulatorProvider] as PROV
  [AvailabilityEmulationContext\nfetchStructure + fetchData] as CTX
  [DataQueryAvailabilityEmulator] as DQE
  [AvailabilityQueryCanonicalizer\nthe single definition of "narrowed"] as CANON
  [UnfilteredConstraintSource] as UCS
  [ProbeQueryBuilder] as PQB
  [ProbeDecomposer] as DEC
  [AvailabilityConstraintSynthesizer] as SYN

  package "harvest" {
    interface SeriesKeyHarvester
    [SeriesKeyHarvesterProvider] as HPROV
    [CsvSeriesKeyHarvester] as CSVH
    [XmlSeriesKeyHarvester] as XMLH
    [JsonSeriesKeyHarvester] as JSONH
    [QueuedResponseDetector] as QRD
    [HarvestedCoverage\nMap<dim, Set<value>> + exact seriesCount] as HC
  }
}

package "sdmx-proxy :: services.cache" {
  [CacheService\n+ get/putEmulatedAvailability] as CACHE
  [CacheKeyGenerator\n+ generateAvailabilityEmulationKey] as CKG
}

package "sdmx-proxy :: services.limit  (design 014)" {
  [LimitEmulationServiceImpl] as LIMIT
  [CodelistSizeResolver] as CSR
}

CTL --> ROUTER
ROUTER --> AEC : reads availabilityEnabled + emulation
ROUTER --> CACHE
ROUTER --> CKG
ROUTER --> PROV
ROUTER --> CTX : constructs
ROUTER --> ADAPTER : only the router talks to the adapter

PROV --> AvailabilityEmulator
DQE ..|> AvailabilityEmulator

DQE --> CANON : route: unfiltered vs narrowed
CKG --> CANON : same predicate -- routing and\ncache identity cannot disagree

DQE --> UCS : UNFILTERED -> the response
DQE --> UCS : NARROWED -> the intersection universe
UCS --> CTX : fetchStructure(contentconstraint | dataconstraint)
UCS --> FIXSVC
UCS --> CONV : convert(XML_STRUCTURE_2_1 -> target)
CONV --> CCM

DQE --> PQB : key + filters carried through unchanged
DQE --> CTX : fetchData(probe)
DQE --> HPROV
DQE --> DEC : only when oversized / timed out
DQE --> SYN
DQE --> CONV : write(Artefacts -> target)

DEC --> CSR : split on the largest UNCONSTRAINED dimension
DEC --> HC : union merge (exact for a rectangular cube region)

HPROV --> SeriesKeyHarvester
CSVH ..|> SeriesKeyHarvester
XMLH ..|> SeriesKeyHarvester
JSONH ..|> SeriesKeyHarvester
SeriesKeyHarvester --> HC
SeriesKeyHarvester --> QRD : detects SOAP <queued> inside a 200

SYN --> HC
FIXSVC --> FIX
LIMIT ..> ADAPTER : availability as a *cheap* probe;\nits probes are always narrowed, so they\nland on the probe path -- ConfigValidator\nforbids the overlap

note bottom of UCS
  Serves the unfiltered request only.
  A NARROWED request is never answered from it --
  not as strategy, not as fallback, not on failure.
  It ignores narrowing (c[] byte-identical, key -> 405),
  so it would report the full cube as narrowed.
end note

note bottom of HC
  Why streaming works: 139 610 759 B / 2 067 919 series
  harvests to 327 strings (BD_9BD_SZ_CL_R2).
  Memory is O(sum |A_d|), bounded by the DSD.
end note

note bottom of CONV
  XML and SDMX 2.1 availability output still throw
  UnsupportedConversionException -- both emulation
  paths share the writer and the limitation.
end note

@enduml
